What type of animal regulates its own body temperature internally? [endotherm | warm-blooded animal | warm blooded animal]

Name the three major body sections of an insect. {head, thorax, abdomen}

A vertebrate is an animal with a [backbone | spine].

What is the process by which animals maintain stable internal conditions called? [homeostasis]

Name two ways mammals usually feed their young. {milk | nursing, suckling | feeding milk}
